TiddlyFlashcards has two parts, installed separately: the TiddlyWiki plugin for creating cards, and the Anki add-on for syncing and reviewing them.

''Before you start:''

* [[TiddlyWiki|https://tiddlywiki.com/]] v5.4.1 or later
* the desktop version of [[Anki|https://apps.ankiweb.net/]] — add-ons are not available in AnkiDroid or AnkiMobile

!! Installation in TiddlyWiki:

!!! 1. Drag and Drop:

# Open the wiki that contains the TiddlyFlashcards plugin in one browser window, and your own wiki in another.
# Drag the ''$:/plugins/uzvg/TiddlyFlashcards'' tiddler into your own wiki. Keep dragging until the drop zone says ''Drop now'', then release.
# In the import dialog, click ''Import''.
# Save your wiki and reload the page.
# Open ''Control Panel'' ➡ ''Plugins''. You should see the ''TiddlyFlashcards'' plugin, marked as ''EXPERIMENTAL''.

<<readme-img img:"$:/plugins/uzvg/TiddlyFlashcards/images/DragAndDropInstallation.png" caption:"Drag & Drop to install TiddlyFlashcards"/>>

!!! 2. For Node.js server users:

With a Node.js server, store the plugin inside the wiki folder.

Copy the ''TiddlyFlashcards'' plugin folder into the ''plugins'' directory of your wiki:

```
<wiki>/plugins/TiddlyFlashcards/
```

Then restart your server (`tiddlywiki <wiki> --listen ...`) and check ''Control Panel'' ➡ ''Plugins''.

For details, see [[Installing custom plugins on Node.js|https://tiddlywiki.com/#Installing%20custom%20plugins%20on%20Node.js]].

!! Installation on Anki:

# [[Install Anki|https://apps.ankiweb.net/]] and launch it.
# Open ''Tools'' ➡ ''Add-ons'' ➡ ''Get Add-ons…''.
# Paste the code `1985067022` and click ''OK''.
# Wait for the add-on to download, then close the add-ons window.
# Restart Anki.

<<readme-img img:"$:/plugins/uzvg/TiddlyFlashcards/images/AnkiInstallAdd-on.png" caption:"Install Anki TiddlyFlashcards Add-on"/>>

Open ''Tools'' ➡ ''Add-ons'' again to confirm that the add-on is listed.

After restarting, open the add-on's config to point it at your TiddlyWiki installation and your wiki. See 👉 <<readme-link index:"2">>.

